      "text": "Prof. Omar Yaghi, UC Berkeley chemist and 2025 Nobel laureate, invented an advanced water harvester using MOFs to extract up to 1,000 L of clean water daily from dry desert air. Through his company Atoco, Yaghi developed compact, off-grid units powered by sunlight or ambient heat—no electricity needed. This sustainable tech, rooted in reticular chemistry, works in low-humidity areas and offers a scalable alternative to energy-intensive, ecologically harmful desalination. Ideal for remote, drought-hit, and disaster-affected regions like the hurricane-prone Caribbean, it supports decentralized water access. Inspired by childhood water scarcity in a Jordanian refugee camp, Yaghi’s work tackles the global crisis with science-driven solutions.\n\n#WaterHarvesting #NobelPrize #Sustainability\n\nFact vortex",
